{"Unused variable results in incorrect monitor context - the function creates a modified copy of the monitor configuration but returns the original unmodified version, so the schedule_type field remains an integer instead of the intended human-readable string": 0.8985695838928223, "Duplicate issue occurrences are created when a monitor first fails - the code incorrectly iterates over all check-ins that contributed to the failure and calls create_incident_occurrence for each one, resulting in multiple identical occurrences instead of a single occurrence for the entire incident": 0.1329323649406433, "Stale object reference passed to downstream function - monitor_env is refreshed from the database but the original failed_checkin object still holds a cached stale reference to monitor_environment, causing try_incident_threshold to operate on out-of-date information like old last_checkin and next_checkin values": 0.4935277998447418}